@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Bảo Minh construction all risks insurance rules ("Quy tắc bảo hiểm mọi rủi ro xây dựng").
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every rule module imports this one.
--
-- Source: ../../source/raw/baominh-car.txt, the `pdftotext -layout` rendering of the
-- 6-page PDF published at baominh.com.vn (PDF sha256 5dbef555...a2bcce), retrieved
-- 2026-10-06. A `src:N` comment quotes line N of that file, generated by
-- `tools/vnsrc.py quote`; nothing Vietnamese here is typed by hand.
--
-- Money is Vietnamese dong (VND), a bare NUMBER. The document prints no money figure at
-- all: every sum, limit, deductible and premium is in the Schedule ("Phụ lục"), which is
-- not part of the document, so each is an input with no default.
--
-- Membership test for this module: a witness of ordinary competence (a site engineer, a
-- loss adjuster, the clerk who keeps the policy file) could testify to the fact. Whether
-- the fact makes Bảo Minh liable is a rule, and belongs in the module of the clause that
-- says so.

§ `Nouns for the construction all risks wording`

§§ `The parties`

-- src:5 | Trên cơ sở Người được bảo hiểm có tên trong phụ lục kèm theo đã gửi cho Tổng Công ty Cổ
DECLARE `A party to the policy` IS ONE OF
    `the Insured`   -- "Người được bảo hiểm", named in the Schedule
    `Bao Minh`      -- "Tổng Công ty Cổ Phần Bảo Minh", the insurer

§§ `The Schedule`

-- The Schedule ("Phụ lục") is not in the document. General Condition 2 makes it part of
-- the Policy:
-- src:62 | 2. Phụ lục và các phần sau được coi là bộ phận cấu thành và nằm trong đơn bảo hiểm và thuật
-- src:63 | ngữ "Đơn bảo hiểm này" dù sử dụng ở chỗ nào trong đơn bảo hiểm này đều được coi là bao
-- Each field below is a figure or date the document tells the reader to look up there.
-- `item number` is the number the Schedule gives the item: the document names "hạng mục 1"
-- (the contract works) and "hạng mục 2 và 3" (construction plant, equipment and machinery)
-- and no other.
-- src:206 | Đối với hạng mục 1: Trị giá đầy đủ của công trình theo hợp đồng tại thời điểm hoàn thành việc xây
-- src:210 | Đối với hạng mục 2 và 3: Trị giá thay thế của trang thiết bị và máy móc xây dựng, tức là chi phí
-- `sum insured` is the sum set against the item, as recorded in the Policy: an increase or
-- decrease the Insured has asked for has no effect until Bảo Minh records it (Article I).
DECLARE `An item entered in the Schedule` HAS
    `item number`  IS A NUMBER
    `description`  IS A STRING
    `sum insured`  IS A NUMBER

-- Section I: the per-item sums, the total sum insured for the Section, a per-occurrence
-- limit of indemnity if the Schedule stipulates one, the separate sum for clearance of
-- debris if the Schedule enters one, and the deductible.
-- (lines 157-160, 162-164 and 173-174)
-- Section II: the limit of indemnity and the deductible.
-- (lines 258, 278-279 and 285)
-- The period: the Schedule states a date; the document says cover begins on site events
-- "whatever date the Schedule states", and ends on the Schedule's date at the latest.
-- (lines 44-45 and 51)
DECLARE `The Schedule` HAS
    `the premium stated in the Schedule`                                IS A NUMBER
    `the date the Schedule states the insurance begins`                 IS A DATE
    `the date the Schedule states the insurance ends`                   IS A DATE
    `the items entered in the Schedule`                                 IS A LIST OF `An item entered in the Schedule`
    `the total sum insured under Section I`                             IS A NUMBER
    `the limit of indemnity for any one occurrence under Section I`     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the separate sum for clearance of debris`                          IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the deductible under Section I for each occurrence`                IS A NUMBER
    `the limit of indemnity under Section II`                           IS A NUMBER
    `the deductible under Section II for each occurrence`               IS A NUMBER

§§ `The policy and the works`

-- What the policy file and the site diary record.
-- * `the premium has been paid`: the insuring clause makes payment of the Schedule premium
--   a condition of indemnity (lines 11-12).
-- * the two site events on which liability commences, each NOTHING until it happens
--   (lines 44-45);
-- * an extension of the period, effective only if agreed by Bảo Minh in writing; NOTHING
--   where none was agreed in writing (lines 51-52);
-- * Article 3: overtime, night work, holiday work and express freight are covered only if
--   specially agreed in writing in advance (lines 252-253).
DECLARE `The policy in force` HAS
    `the Schedule`                                                                      IS A `The Schedule`
    `the premium has been paid`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date work on the site commenced`                                               IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date the items entered in the Schedule were unloaded at the site`              IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the end date of an extension agreed by Bao Minh in writing`                        IS A MAYBE DATE
    `overtime, night work, holiday work and express freight were agreed in writing in advance` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The Insured's conduct of the risk (General Conditions 1, 3, 4 and 6)`

-- Each field is a fact about what the Insured did or did not do while on risk.
-- General Condition 1 makes compliance with every duty, and true answers in the
-- questionnaire and the proposal, a condition precedent to Bảo Minh's liability (lines
-- 57-60). The duties are General Conditions 3 (lines 68-70), 4 (lines 72-84) and 6
-- (lines 117-124); each is encoded in bmcar-general-conditions.l4.
-- `there was a material change in the risk` is the trigger for General Condition 4(b);
-- the two fields after it are read only when it is TRUE.
DECLARE `The Insured's conduct of the risk` HAS
    `the answers in the questionnaire and the proposal were true`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `took every reasonable precaution and followed Bao Minh's reasonable recommendations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `complied with the regulations and the manufacturer's recommendations`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `gave Bao Minh's representatives the details and information needed to assess the risk` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there was a material change in the risk`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `notified the material change immediately, by telegram and in writing`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `took the additional precautions the change required`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `made or admitted a material change increasing the risk without Bao Minh's written approval` IS A BOOLEAN
    `did and permitted the acts Bao Minh required to enforce rights against third parties` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The notice of an occurrence and the Insured's conduct after it (General Condition 5)`

-- General Condition 5 (lines 86-104), encoded in bmcar-general-conditions.l4.
-- `the date Bao Minh received the notice`: NOTHING where no notice of the loss has been
-- received. The 14-day bar runs to RECEIPT ("Bảo Minh không nhận được thông báo").
DECLARE `The notice of an occurrence` HAS
    `the date Bao Minh received the notice`                IS A MAYBE DATE
    `given immediately`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `by telephone or telegram`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `in writing`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `stating the nature and extent of the loss`             IS A BOOLEAN

-- General Condition 5, last paragraphs (lines 106-112), and Section II Condition 1
-- (lines 312-319).
-- `repaired, before an inspection, damage that was not minor`: TRUE only where the
-- Insured repaired or replaced non-minor damage before Bảo Minh's representative inspected
-- it AND before a period reasonable in the circumstances had passed without an inspection.
DECLARE `The Insured's conduct after the occurrence` HAS
    `the notice`                                                                         IS A `The notice of an occurrence`
    `took all steps within its power to minimise the loss`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `preserved the damaged parts and made them available for inspection`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `furnished the information and documents Bao Minh required`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `informed the police`                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `repaired, before an inspection, damage that was not minor`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `made an admission, offer, promise or payment without Bao Minh's written consent`    IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Causes`

-- What brought the loss about, as a list: the General Exclusions reach a loss caused
-- "directly or indirectly" by a named risk, so one loss may have several causes.
-- src:19 | Bảo Minh sẽ không bồi thường cho Người được bảo hiểm những thiệt hại hoặc những trách nhiệm
-- src:20 | trực tiếp hay gián tiếp gây nên bởi các rủi ro sau:
-- General Exclusion (a) (lines 22-28), in six groups of the risks it lists; General
-- Exclusions (b), (c), (d) (lines 30-34); Section I exclusions (c), (e), (f) (lines 179 and
-- 186-190); Section II exclusions 3 and 4(c) (lines 290-292 and 304-305); theft, which
-- General Condition 5(e) names (line 100).
-- `defective material or workmanship in the item itself` is read only by the alternative
-- reading of Section I exclusion (d) (NOTES.md, finding X14); the reading taken works on
-- the cost of rectifying the defect, a field of `A loss to an item`.
DECLARE `A cause` IS ONE OF
    `war, invasion, act of foreign enemies or hostilities, whether war be declared or not`
    `civil war, rebellion, revolution, insurrection or mutiny`
    `riot, strike, lock-out or civil commotion`
    `military or usurped power`
    `the acts of hostile persons acting for or in connection with a political organisation`
    `confiscation, requisition or destruction by order of a government de jure or de facto or of any public authority`
    `nuclear reaction, nuclear radiation or radioactive contamination`
    `a wilful act or wilful negligence of the Insured or its representatives`
    `cessation of work, whole or partial`
    `faulty design`
    `defective material or workmanship in the item itself`
    `corrosion, wear, oxidation or deterioration due to lack of use or normal pressure and temperature`
    `mechanical or electrical breakdown or derangement of construction plant, equipment or machinery`
    `vibration or the removal or weakening of support`
    `damage to property, land or buildings caused by vibration or by the removal or weakening of support`
    `an accident caused by a vehicle licensed for public roads, or by a ship, barge or aircraft`
    `theft`
    `a cause the policy does not name, namely` HAS `description` IS A STRING

§§ `What the lost or damaged property is (Section I exclusions (g) and (h))`

-- Section I exclusions (g) and (h) (lines 192-196).
-- `construction plant, equipment or machinery` is listed because Section I exclusion (f)
-- reaches the breakdown OF such plant (the reading taken, fork F24).
DECLARE `A kind of property` IS ONE OF
    `the contract works or other property of an ordinary kind`
    `construction plant, equipment or machinery`
    `a motor vehicle licensed for use on public roads`
    `a ship`
    `a barge`
    `files`
    `drawings`
    `accounting records`
    `bills or invoices`
    `cash`
    `stamps or coupons`
    `documents`
    `evidences of debt`
    `share certificates`
    `letters of guarantee`
    `cheques`

§§ `A loss to an item (Section I)`

-- Article 2 values the loss on one of two bases, (a) repairable and (b) total loss.
-- (lines 225-232)
-- For a repairable loss, the adjuster states the cost necessary to restore the item to its
-- condition immediately before the occurrence.
DECLARE `The state of the item after the occurrence` IS ONE OF
    `repairable, at a necessary cost of` HAS `the cost necessary to restore the item to its condition immediately before the occurrence` IS A NUMBER
    `a total loss`

-- Article I: the value the sum insured is tested against. For item 1, the full contract
-- value of the works at completion, including what the principal ("bên A") supplied
-- (lines 206-208).
-- `the contract value ...` is the contract price at completion, with the materials, wages,
-- freight, customs duties and other taxes the clause names; `the value of materials or
-- items supplied by the principal` is what the principal supplies and the contract price
-- does not already contain (fork F25).
DECLARE `The full contract value of the works at completion` HAS
    `the contract value at completion, with all materials, wages, freight, customs duties and other taxes` IS A NUMBER
    `the value of materials or items supplied by the principal`                                         IS A NUMBER

-- One item's loss in one occurrence. The fields in order:
-- * the item, as entered in the Schedule; what the property is; the Section I insuring
--   clause's three qualities of the loss (lines 152-155);
-- * the causes, for the General Exclusions and Section I exclusions (c), (e), (f);
-- * `discovered only when an inventory was taken`, Section I exclusion (i) (line 198);
-- * the two facts on which the period ends for a part of the works, and the fact that ends
--   cover for an item damaged earlier and not repaired properly without delay (lines
--   47-48 and 114-115);
-- * the Article 2 valuation: the state of the item, its actual value immediately before
--   the occurrence, salvage, and what the Insured has actually incurred, broken down so
--   that Articles 2 and 3 and Section I exclusion (d) can each take their part out of it
--   (lines 234-236, 244-248, 252-253 and 181-184);
-- * whether the invoices and documents showing the repair or replacement were produced
--   (lines 238-240);
-- * Article I: the value the sum insured is tested against, for the item's kind. NOTHING
--   where it has not been established; the rule that needs it then declines by name
--   (lines 206-211 and 217-220).
DECLARE `A loss to an item` HAS
    `the item`                                                                  IS AN `An item entered in the Schedule`
    `what the property is`                                                      IS A `A kind of property`
    `physical loss or damage`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `sudden and unforeseen`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `to an extent that requires repair or replacement`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the causes`                                                                IS A LIST OF `A cause`
    `discovered only when an inventory was taken`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the damaged part had been handed over before the occurrence`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the damaged part had been put into use before the occurrence`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `damaged in an earlier occurrence and not then repaired properly without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the state after the occurrence`                                            IS A `The state of the item after the occurrence`
    `the actual value immediately before the occurrence`                        IS A NUMBER
    `the value of salvage`                                                      IS A NUMBER
    `the cost the Insured has actually incurred in repairing or replacing it`   IS A NUMBER
    `of which, alterations, additions or improvements`                          IS A NUMBER
    `of which, overtime, night work, holiday work or express freight`           IS A NUMBER
    `of which, provisional repairs not part of the final repairs or increasing their cost` IS A NUMBER
    `of which, replacing, repairing or rectifying defective material or workmanship` IS A NUMBER
    `the part of the loss not included in the sum insured`                      IS A NUMBER
    `the invoices and documents showing the repair or replacement were produced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the full contract value of the works at completion`                        IS A MAYBE `The full contract value of the works at completion`
    `the replacement value by a new item of the same kind and capacity`         IS A MAYBE NUMBER

§§ `The history of a claim (General Conditions 7 and 8)`

-- General Condition 7 (lines 126-134).
DECLARE `Who made an award` IS ONE OF
    `a single arbitrator appointed by both parties`
    `the two arbitrators`
    `the umpire appointed by the two arbitrators`

DECLARE `An arbitral award` HAS
    `made by`             IS A `Who made an award`
    `the date of the award` IS A DATE

-- General Condition 8: fraud, a false declaration, fraudulent means, and the time-bar
-- after an award (lines 136-141). `as at` is the date on which the question is asked.
DECLARE `The history of a claim` HAS
    `the claim is fraudulent`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a false declaration was made or used in support of the claim`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `fraudulent means or devices were used by or for the Insured to obtain a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim was rejected`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the award`                                                                 IS A MAYBE `An arbitral award`
    `the date proceedings were commenced`                                       IS A MAYBE DATE
    `as at`                                                                     IS A DATE

§§ `A claim under Section I`

-- One occurrence ("sự cố"), the items it damaged, and what is claimed besides.
-- * `the cost of clearance of debris`: the cost after the occurrence (lines 162-164);
-- * `the consequential losses claimed`: penalties, delay, non-performance, loss of contract
--   (lines 176-177);
-- * `Section I indemnity already paid in the period`: for the aggregate limit (lines
--   159-160);
-- * `another insurance covers the same loss`: General Condition 9 (lines 143-145).
DECLARE `A claim under Section I` HAS
    `the date of the occurrence`                          IS A DATE
    `the losses to items`                                 IS A LIST OF `A loss to an item`
    `the cost of clearance of debris`                     IS A NUMBER
    `the consequential losses claimed`                    IS A NUMBER
    `Section I indemnity already paid in the period`      IS A NUMBER
    `another insurance covers the same loss`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Insured's conduct after the occurrence`          IS A `The Insured's conduct after the occurrence`
    `the history of the claim`                            IS A `The history of a claim`

§§ `A claim under Section II`

-- src:262 | a) thương tật hay ốm đau bất ngờ cho bên thứ ba (dù chết hay không)
-- src:264 | b) tổn thất bất ngờ đối với tài sản thuộc bên thứ ba,
DECLARE `What the third party suffered` IS ONE OF
    `bodily injury or illness, fatal or not`
    `loss of or damage to property belonging to the third party`

-- One third-party claim arising from one occurrence. The fields in order:
-- * the occurrence, what the third party suffered, and the insuring clause's qualities;
-- * the causes (General Exclusions; Section II exclusions 3 and 4(c));
-- * Section II exclusion 3's endorsement proviso (line 292);
-- * Section II exclusions 4(a), 4(b), 4(d) (lines 294-308);
-- * legal liability, the damages, and the part of them that Section II exclusion 2 takes
--   out (lines 287-288); the two heads of costs (lines 269-273).
DECLARE `A claim under Section II` HAS
    `the date of the occurrence`                                               IS A DATE
    `what the third party suffered`                                            IS A `What the third party suffered`
    `accidental`                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `in direct connection with the construction or erection of the items insured under Section I` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on or in the immediate vicinity of the site`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the causes`                                                               IS A LIST OF `A cause`
    `the vibration and support exclusion has been varied by endorsement`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injured person is an employee or worker of the contractor, the principal or a firm connected with the works, or of their family` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the property belongs to or is in the care, custody or control of the contractor, the principal, a firm connected with the works, or an employee or worker of one of them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the liability arises from an agreement of the Insured to pay by way of indemnity or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the liability would have attached in the absence of that agreement`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Insured is legally liable to pay damages`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the damages the Insured is legally liable to pay`                         IS A NUMBER
    `of which, expenditure on doing, redoing, making good, repairing or replacing anything insured or insurable under Section I` IS A NUMBER
    `the claimant's costs and expenses of litigation recovered from the Insured` IS A NUMBER
    `costs and expenses incurred with the written consent of Bao Minh`         IS A NUMBER
    `another insurance covers the same liability`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Insured's conduct after the occurrence`                               IS A `The Insured's conduct after the occurrence`
    `the history of the claim`                                                 IS A `The history of a claim`

§§ `Outcomes`

-- What a claim comes to. The reasons are the document's own, each with its clause; a
-- claim the encoding cannot answer is not here, it is a REFUSE.
DECLARE `A reason nothing is payable` IS ONE OF
    `the premium stated in the Schedule has not been paid`
    `General Condition 8 — all benefit under the Policy is forfeited`
    `General Condition 1 — a condition precedent to liability is not met`
    `General Condition 5 — Bao Minh did not receive notice within 14 days of the occurrence`
    `no loss claimed is within the cover`

DECLARE `The outcome of a claim` IS ONE OF
    `nothing is payable, because` HAS `the reason` IS A `A reason nothing is payable`
    `payable`                     HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Acts the regulative clauses speak of`

-- The acts the deontic clauses (General Conditions 5 and 7, Section II Condition 1)
-- oblige, permit or forbid.
-- (lines 89-90, 106-112, 128-131, 139-141 and 312-317)
DECLARE `An act under the policy` IS ONE OF
    `give notice of the occurrence that Bao Minh receives`
    `inspect the loss`
    `repair or replace the damaged item`
    `appoint an arbitrator in writing`
    `make an admission, offer, promise or payment without Bao Minh's written consent`
    `take over and conduct the defence or settlement of the claim in the Insured's name`
    `commence proceedings against Bao Minh`
